{:edb/db-before-t 2294 :edb/db-after-t 2295 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535607 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:26:28.485Z" 13194139535607 true] [17592186121555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357312 13194139535607 true] [17592186121555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357313 13194139535607 true] [17592186121555 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357312 13194139535607 true] [17592186121556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357315 13194139535607 true] [17592186121556 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357315 13194139535607 true] [17592186121557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357314 13194139535607 true] [17592186121557 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357314 13194139535607 true] [17592186121558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357316 13194139535607 true] [17592186121558 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357316 13194139535607 true] [17592186121559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357317 13194139535607 true] [17592186121559 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357317 13194139535607 true] [17592186124417 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357331 13194139535607 true] [17592186124418 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357318 13194139535607 true] [17592186124756 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535607 true] [17592186124756 1100 "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $PQ^(―)$, where $P(1, 4,-2)$ and $Q(-2, 3, 1)$.\n\n| $x =$ | {{field-1}} | $[MATH: t ∈ [0,]$ {{field-2}} $[MATH:]]$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $y =$ | $4 - t$ |  |\n| $z =$ | {{field-3}} |  |" 13194139535607 false] [17592186124756 1100 "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(-2,3,1).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [0,$ {{field-2}} $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $4-t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | {{field-3}} |  |" 13194139535607 true] [17592186124756 1145 "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3t \\\\ -t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+3t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-3t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$" 13194139535607 true] [17592186124757 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535607 true] [17592186124757 1100 "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $PQ^(―)$, where $P(-5, 7, 1)$ and $Q(-4,-1, 6)$.\n\n| $x =$ | {{field-1}} | $[MATH: t ∈ []$ {{field-2}} $[MATH:, 1]]$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $y =$ | $7 - 8t$ |  |\n| $z =$ | $1 + 5t$ |  |" 13194139535607 false] [17592186124757 1100 "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(-5,7,1)$ and $Q(-4,-1,6).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [$ {{field-2}} $,1]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $7-8t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | $1+5t$ |  |" 13194139535607 true] [17592186124757 1145 "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ -8t \\\\ 5t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5+t \\\\ 7-8t \\\\ 1+5t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-5+t \\\\ y=7-8t \\\\ z=1+5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$" 13194139535607 true] [17592186124866 1017 #edb/ref 17592186122218 13194139535607 false] [17592186124866 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357325 13194139535607 true] [17592186124866 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535607 true] [17592186124866 1100 "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(1, 4,-2)$ and $Q(5, 3, 0)$." 13194139535607 false] [17592186124866 1100 "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$" 13194139535607 true] [17592186124866 1145 "We know that the line passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1+4t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535607 true] [17592186357312 1034 "1-3t" 13194139535607 true] [17592186357312 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535607 true] [17592186357312 1111 #uuid "a73fe140-3a26-5c33-b76d-7182da90c8b3" 13194139535607 true] [17592186357313 1034 "1+3t" 13194139535607 true] [17592186357313 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535607 true] [17592186357313 1111 #uuid "979248b0-67ce-5295-b739-98d0f9c9a5dd" 13194139535607 true] [17592186357314 1034 "1" 13194139535607 true] [17592186357314 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535607 true] [17592186357314 1111 #uuid "9daa492b-2b2f-5a2a-870c-36a8804a3e44" 13194139535607 true] [17592186357315 1034 "-2+3t" 13194139535607 true] [17592186357315 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535607 true] [17592186357315 1111 #uuid "e8caaea8-b523-5b0a-9fd8-80d04d8092a5" 13194139535607 true] [17592186357316 1034 "-5+t" 13194139535607 true] [17592186357316 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535607 true] [17592186357316 1111 #uuid "2a3199e0-7ca6-5317-9afa-2d99c3b3771e" 13194139535607 true] [17592186357317 1034 "0" 13194139535607 true] [175921863